{"kind":"comment","author":"agent","agent":"Codex","session":"01a0bfe4-a7f6-7321-937f-c62fa8c99431","revision":1,"text":"Workshop planning: how should we use the afternoon?","anchor":{"section":"bg-thread-checkpoint"},"id":"9ee465bb3f9c1fa309ea9cb1767fa365","ts":"2026-09-21T09:19:59-07:00"}
{"kind":"conversation_title","author":"agent","agent":"Codex","conversation":"9ee465bb3f9c1fa309ea9cb1767fa365","title":"Afternoon workshop","id":"99a9002058ea44edb0b5a2bec52bdd06","ts":"2026-09-21T09:19:59-07:00"}
{"kind":"reply","author":"user","parent":"9ee465bb3f9c1fa309ea9cb1767fa365","text":"Use the afternoon for hands-on practice rather than more presentations.","revision":1,"id":"9084b9141a1ac15fd58de1bd60d04739","ts":"2026-09-21T09:20:25-07:00"}
{"kind":"reply","author":"agent","parent":"9ee465bb3f9c1fa309ea9cb1767fa365","text":"I suggest two small groups, each working through a real debugging case. We can keep the introduction to fifteen minutes.","agent":"Codex","session":"01a0bfe4-a7f6-7321-937f-c62fa8c99431","responds":"9084b9141a1ac15fd58de1bd60d04739","id":"6ab388f0f80d0cb5e099efddb7d3e252","ts":"2026-09-21T09:20:25-07:00"}
{"kind":"reply","author":"user","parent":"9ee465bb3f9c1fa309ea9cb1767fa365","text":"People have different experience levels. Pair a newcomer with somebody who knows the tools.","revision":1,"id":"34c1ac13fcbffb10183d20636882ba6c","ts":"2026-09-21T09:20:25-07:00"}
{"kind":"reply","author":"agent","parent":"9ee465bb3f9c1fa309ea9cb1767fa365","text":"Mixed-experience pairs should work. Each pair can choose a case, reproduce it, and explain the fix to the other group.","agent":"Codex","session":"01a0bfe4-a7f6-7321-937f-c62fa8c99431","responds":"34c1ac13fcbffb10183d20636882ba6c","id":"76bbf893eb4598102b9c78840e3e0184","ts":"2026-09-21T09:20:25-07:00"}
{"kind":"reply","author":"user","parent":"9ee465bb3f9c1fa309ea9cb1767fa365","text":"Keep a break between practice and the group discussion. We will need time to compare notes.","revision":1,"id":"2fe91bb1d8af9b715a8e73c47774dc60","ts":"2026-09-21T09:20:25-07:00"}
{"kind":"reply","author":"agent","parent":"9ee465bb3f9c1fa309ea9cb1767fa365","text":"The afternoon now has a short introduction, paired practice, a break, and a closing discussion. The facilitator will bring two cases.","agent":"Codex","session":"01a0bfe4-a7f6-7321-937f-c62fa8c99431","responds":"2fe91bb1d8af9b715a8e73c47774dc60","id":"09c7dad37f9b1c04567b417d3861d667","ts":"2026-09-21T09:20:25-07:00"}
{"kind":"reply","author":"user","parent":"9ee465bb3f9c1fa309ea9cb1767fa365","text":"What should people prepare before arriving?","revision":1,"id":"377b66b12918701c7aef251f31e6d2b7","ts":"2026-09-21T09:20:25-07:00"}
{"kind":"summary","author":"agent","agent":"Codex","session":"01a0bfe4-a7f6-7321-937f-c62fa8c99431","conversation":"9ee465bb3f9c1fa309ea9cb1767fa365","from":"9ee465bb3f9c1fa309ea9cb1767fa365","through":"09c7dad37f9b1c04567b417d3861d667","text":"The afternoon will focus on **hands-on debugging in mixed-experience pairs**. A fifteen-minute introduction leads into practice with two facilitator-supplied cases, followed by a break and a group discussion.","id":"7cf2d9105e0c54198727f18a4da7d6fd","ts":"2026-09-21T09:21:00-07:00"}
{"kind":"reply","author":"agent","parent":"9ee465bb3f9c1fa309ea9cb1767fa365","text":"Bring a laptop with the workshop tools installed and one small bug or confusing trace to investigate. No advance debugging is needed.","agent":"Codex","session":"01a0bfe4-a7f6-7321-937f-c62fa8c99431","responds":"377b66b12918701c7aef251f31e6d2b7","id":"b2d6c324091f5e287fd34b89dcfa5ab4","ts":"2026-09-21T09:21:01-07:00"}
